1. Definitions

   "Licensor" means Runlot and its successors.

   "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
   license. For a legal entity, "You" includes every entity under common
   control with it, where "control" means ownership of more than fifty
   percent of voting interests or the power to direct management.

   "Production Use" means use of the Software other than for development,
   testing, evaluation, education, research or demonstration.

   "Annual Revenue" means the total gross revenue of You, measured over the
   most recently completed fiscal year, in all currencies converted to United
   States dollars at the average exchange rate of that year.

   "Revenue Threshold" means ten million United States dollars
   (USD 10,000,000; about KRW 14,000,000,000 as of 2026).

   "Database Service" means a commercial offering that allows third parties
   (other than Your employees and contractors) to access the functionality of
   the Software by creating databases or tables whose schemas are controlled
   by those third parties.

   "Change Date" means, for each version of the Software, the fourth
   anniversary of the date the Licensor first publicly distributes that
   version.

   "Commercial License" means a separate written agreement with the Licensor
   granting rights beyond this license.

