3. Conditions

   (a) Production Use is free of charge if You are an individual acting on
       Your own behalf, an educational or academic institution, a non-profit
       organisation, or an organisation whose Annual Revenue is below the
       Revenue Threshold.

   (b) If Your Annual Revenue is at or above the Revenue Threshold, Production
       Use requires a Commercial License. You may evaluate the Software for
       Production Use for thirty days without one.

   (c) The Revenue Threshold is assessed when You first make Production Use
       of a given version of the Software. If You were below the Threshold at
       that time, crossing it later does not require a Commercial License for
       that version; it applies to the next version You adopt.

   (d) You must retain this license, the NOTICE file and all copyright and
       attribution notices in every copy or substantial portion of the
       Software and in any derivative work, and You must make this license
       conspicuously available to anyone You distribute the Software or a
       derivative work to. A derivative work distributed by You is subject to
       this license.

4. Exclusion

   Regardless of Annual Revenue, You may not use the Software to provide a
   Database Service without a Commercial License. For clarity, running the
   Software inside Your own applications, for Your own organisation, or
   embedded in a product You distribute where the schemas are controlled by
   You and not by the product's users, is not a Database Service.

5. Commercial Licenses

